Z||000007||Fierowrecker||09-30-2001||02:47 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by maryjane:<BR><B>Noble, thought provoking and inspiring words, especially in these troubled times. I've just seen too many able bodied men standing on the side of the road with the "need work, family to feed, disabled vet"<BR>signs, to get too upset anymore. I've offered some of em jobs, they refuse. This is a true story that happened to me, kinda long & a little funny:<BR>I'm fishing one day here in San Angelo in a small river, not much bigger than a stream, but pretty deep. It starts raining, so I move under a bridge  nearby, and continue fishing. Looking up under the bridge across the river, I see a homeless guy laying down, I see he is watching me. It's hot as hell & I wonder how he's  making it. I think about the $ I've spent on bait ,ice & beer for the fishing & feel a little guilty. I reel in my line, remove the minnow, fold up a $5 bill, and hook it on. I cast it up to the other side. He doesn't move much. I yell over that there is a 5 dollar bill on the hook. He looks down toward it, and says,"can you come over the bridge & give it to me? It's too hot to get up & come down there." It's only about 15 feet to the hook & line, & pouring down rain too much to go out & cross the bridge. I think the hell with this lazy ass, & just jerk the rod back, to avoid dragging the bill thru the water. The hook,$5, & sinker come flying back & hit me squarely in the forehead & face. He's laughin & I didn't feel guilty anymore. He just lays back down & goes back to sleep.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Reminds me of a trip to Ontario...<BR>Panhandlers all over the place, didn't give a dime to them, but to the homeless guy sleeping in the subway staircase, I gave to him...<BR>Where all the others went after sundown, who knows?<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000008||Fleabitdog||09-30-2001||10:53 AM||||I was homeless for about 4years. I thumbed it from Pa to Fl in 1980 because I beleived I would be homeless for the rest of my life.At least Fl would be warm. There was a time in Fl that all I had to my name was a pair of brown corduroys. I did not have any sign or ask for money. I slept under bridges and in alleys and the woods. I hung out at bars and would do sde work whenever I could find some so I could do my drinking or drugging. Food did not matter as much as drinking or drugging. I was homeless because I would rather get high ordrink then pay rent.I did not own a car for probably about six years because I could not keep even 20 bucks in my pocket. I wa healthy, I could of worked. Friends and family tried to tell me I had a problem for many years. I did not beleive them. Finally in Sept of 87, I hit my bottom. I admitted I had a problem and asked for help. I don't live outside anymore. There are some unfortunate who rally cannot help thier situation but there are also many as in my case that don't need the pity or enabling. If I see someone that I beleive really needs my help, I will help them. If I see someone that reminds me of me, the best I can do is offer to take them for a meal, cup of coffee, tell them my experince, offer to take them to a meeting or a detox and to be thier friend. Dave<P>[This message has been edited by Fleabitdog (edited 09-30-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by Fleabitdog (edited 09-30-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||hugh||09-30-2001||11:57 AM||||Dave,Congratulations.I only quit smoking and I know how hard that was to do.I have a friend that has been sober for 2 years,and I have nothing but admiration for him and people that have gone through what you have.Again,congratulations!!!||||reg||7
Z||000010||maryjane||09-30-2001||12:11 PM||||You're right Hugh, I saw a sign or something once that said 'non-addicts can never understand". Been trying to quit smoking for several years. Fleabitdog, you're a courageous person to post your experiences with homelesness. I have trouble admitting my smallest faults/problems. Hats off to ya.||||reg||14
Z||000011||Formula88||09-30-2001||12:57 PM||||I guess I've become cynical, mainly because it seems like getting hit up for money is the cost of walking across the street down town.  Too many of them are just hustlers trying to get a buck.  I've also seen examples of people begging for money and making good money at it.  A local TV crew interviewed one beggar who said this was "his job" and how he chose to make his living.  Well that's fine and all, but I want to see the taxes he pays on his handouts, if that's his income.<P>Today, if I think someone is in need, I'll try to help.  I'll buy them some food, whatever.  But every single time I've offered to buy someone food (someone who's just asked for money because they haven't eaten in x days) they always get pissed off and just want the money.  I'm tired of being hustled.  I had a good friend of mine was homeless for several years, and in all that time, he never had the need to beg for money.  He could always get by picking up odd work, etc.  <P>The last time I did give someone money, was a drunk came up to me and my friends and asked for some money so he could go get drunk.  He was honest.  It may not have been the right thing to do, but my friends and I gave him some money simply because he didn't B.S. us.  <P>This is nothing new.  During the depression in the 30's, people would frequently come up to my grandmother's house and ask for a handout.  Since she didn't have money to spare, she couldn't give them anything, but if they wanted some food, she'd fix them something to eat.  Most of them walked away when they couldn't get money, but a few would take her up on the food.  Even stopping to sit on her front steps and eat whatever it was she fixed before going on their way.  <P>It's hard to do sometimes.  I don't like getting hustled, but I would want to help someone who really needed it.  <P>Sorry for the long rant.  ||||reg||1
Z||000012||California Kid||09-30-2001||01:48 PM||||FleaBitDog: Dave, My hat is off to ya bud, you have accomplished what very few people can. I can't imagine what you must have gone through!!! Best Wishes for the Future.||||reg||1
